      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can make this read a little better and explain the Codex case so it\u0027s future proofed\n```suggestion\nFix tool pre-approval in the Gerrit task query skill\n\nGerrit task queries still require permission prompts in Claude Code,\nblocking headless sessions despite the skill\u0027s allowed-tools list.\nThe bare mcp__gerrit__ prefix does not match plugin-bundled tools.\n\nUse mcp__plugin_gerrit_gerrit__ for all five allowed MCP tools to match\nthe names Claude Code exposes through the Gerrit plugin.\n\nCodex recognizes bare names such as mcp__gerrit__get_change_details,\nbut ignores allowed-tools for permission grants, even with an MCP\nserver dependency declared in agents/openai.yaml. Using Claude Code\u0027s\nplugin-scoped names therefore does not affect Codex permissions.\n\nIn a headless session (claude -p, default permission mode) with the\nskill loaded, Claude Code 2.1.303 refused get_change_details and\nget_task_tree before this change. With the updated list, both calls\ncompleted without a permission prompt.\n```",
